  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "69999272-c330-4231-95ca-b1c853630c5b",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -6112,
        5392
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 1120,
        "content": "## AI DevOps Incident Management System\n\n### How it works\n1. A Slack message or forwarded alert triggers the workflow.\n2. An AI agent investigates using Prometheus, Loki, and a RAG search over past incidents, then writes a structured Root Cause Analysis.\n3. Every analysis is logged to Postgres for audit history.\n4. If a remediation is proposed, a human must approve it in Slack before anything touches real infrastructure.\n5. Once approved, the workflow files a ticket, applies the fix via Terraform, and verifies resolution with Prometheus and Grafana.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Add Slack credentials (trigger + bot token)\n- [ ] Add an OpenAI credential and a Vector Store credential for the RAG tool\n- [ ] Add HTTP credentials for Prometheus and Loki\n- [ ] Add a Postgres credential and create the `incidents` table\n- [ ] Add Jira or GitHub credentials on whichever ticketing node you keep\n- [ ] Add Terraform Cloud/Enterprise API credentials\n- [ ] Point the approval Wait node's resume webhook at your Slack interactive-message action\n\n### Customization\nSwap Jira for GitHub Issues (or vice versa) by deleting the unused branch off the ticketing switch."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d7a620c5-5236-46cb-9f56-4176a4d68c36",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Trigger & Agent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4928,
        5376
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 1328,
        "content": "## Trigger and investigate\n\nCaptures the incident report from Slack, then has an AI agent pull metrics, logs, and past-incident context to build a root cause analysis."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "761d6b12-cb73-4cce-acc2-56b42c5e1b09",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Persistence & Gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4096,
        5424
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1360,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## Log analysis and get approval\n\nSaves every analysis for audit history, then routes to a human approval step in Slack whenever a concrete remediation is proposed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4ae9170c-fef8-4f50-a922-907d49443092",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Remediation & Verification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2672,
