    {
      "id": "05a60a66-4ba7-490b-9da2-50005bf38d72",
      "name": "AI Agent - Incident Investigator",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "position": [
        -4400,
        5888
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=You are a senior Site Reliability Engineer investigating a production incident reported in Slack.\n\nIncident report:\n\"{{ $json.incidentText }}\"\n\nReported by: {{ $json.reportedBy }}\n\nYou have three tools: query_prometheus (metrics), query_loki (logs), search_past_incidents (RAG over past postmortems/runbooks). Use whichever combination is relevant — call multiple tools, and call them more than once with refined queries, before concluding. Do not guess metrics or log content; only state what the tools returned.\n\nIf earlier turns exist in this conversation (same Slack thread), treat this as a follow-up about the SAME incident and use that context.\n\nAssign a riskLevel to any proposed remediation: 'low' (config/read-only change), 'medium' (scaling/restart), or 'high' (infra topology change, data migration, anything hard to reverse). If you do not yet have enough evidence for a confident root cause, leave proposedRemediation empty and explain what further investigation is needed in summary instead.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object (no markdown fences, no commentary) with keys: summary (2-4 sentences), rootCause (string, empty if not yet determined), confidence ('low'|'medium'|'high'), evidence (array of strings citing what Prometheus/Loki/RAG returned), proposedRemediation (string, empty if none), riskLevel ('low'|'medium'|'high'|''), affectedService (string).",
        "options": {},
        "promptType": "define"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.6
    },
    {
